---
title: "Create a tabular export preset"
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

Save a repeatable record selection, field mapping, and header configuration.

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Open `Settings` > `Tabular Data`.
2. Create a preset and give it a descriptive name.
3. Choose the record type, taxon scope, and field mode.
4. Add and order fields, then configure standard mappings or custom headers.
5. Field and setting changes save automatically. To change the name, type it and select `Rename`.
6. Test the preset through `Export records` with representative data.
{% /steps %}

{% aside type="tip" %}
Export one preset from its row, or all of them from the options menu. Both write the same file, so either imports through the same `Import` action.
{% /aside %}

